BananaOS's RetroArch patch 0001 (buildroot/patches/retroarch), what ROCKNIX's RetroArch lacks of it (it has the
AUDIO_REINIT command already): alsa-lib's configuration read again when the ALSA driver opens, so a driver opened
again plays where "default" goes now (headphones, a Bluetooth speaker through PipeWire's ALSA plugin).

diff --git a/audio/drivers/alsa.c b/audio/drivers/alsa.c
index c3208be..bbf2142 100644
--- a/audio/drivers/alsa.c
+++ b/audio/drivers/alsa.c
@@ -500,6 +500,9 @@ static void *alsa_init(const char *device, unsigned rate, unsigned latency,
    RARCH_LOG("[ALSA] Using ALSA version %s.\n", snd_asoundlib_version());
 
    alsa->requested_layout = audio_driver_requested_layout();
+   /* alsa-lib reads its configuration once per process; a device opened again (AUDIO_REINIT) goes where
+    * "default" is now, so the configuration read so far is forgotten first */
+   snd_config_update_free_global();
    if (alsa_init_pcm(&alsa->pcm, device, SND_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK, rate,
             latency, audio_layout_channels(alsa->requested_layout),
             &alsa->stream_info, new_rate, SND_PCM_NONBLOCK) < 0)
